-- title:
--   Crossing normal form descends along prime-to-p level raising
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field `x1FunctionField (M * p)` of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating the maximal ideal, and acting on $K$ compatibly. Let $j\in K$ be an element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of `jq`, assumed nonzero, and let $X$ be [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two Spec's of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of the pullback of $\varpi$ along `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y$ be a point of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite chart mapping to $z$, and assume $y$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the $j$-finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet p`$\Omega$, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic Weierstrass models over $\Omega$ have no nonzero $p$-torsion affine point. Let further $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid Mp$, let $K'$ be the corresponding field for `x1FunctionField (M * ℓ * p)` with $K\le K'$ and compatible $A$-action, let $j'\in K'$ be nonzero with the same Laurent expansion, let $\iota$ be an $A$-algebra map between the two $j$-finite chart algebras compatible with the inclusions into $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and let $z'$, $y'$ be points of the model $X'$ over $M\ell p$ and of its $j$-finite chart with $y'\mapsto z'$ and $\iota^{-1}(y')=y$. Assume the crossing normal form at $z'$: there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with maximal ideal of $W$ generated by $\sigma\varpi$, and a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk of $X'$ at $z'$ onto `UVCrossingModel W (σ ϖ)` carrying, for every $a\in A$, the image of the germ of the pullback of $a$ to the constant `UVCrossingModel.const (σ ϖ) (σ a)`. The conclusion is the same assertion with $(X',z')$ replaced by $(X,z)$: such $W$, $\sigma$ and an isomorphism of the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ with `UVCrossingModel W (σ ϖ)`, compatible with constants from $A$, exist.
--
--   This is the descent step for the local structure of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ at a supersingular point of the characteristic-$p$ fibre: the crossing (two-branch) normal form $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi)$ for the completed local ring at a supersingular point is transported from level $M\ell p$ down to level $Mp$ across a prime-to-$p$ raising of the level. It feeds the statement deriving the same normal form from non-regularity of the fibre at the point.
-- source:
